  "observations": [
    "New C0/C1/C2 queries delegate to public OpenNURBS through the existing owned constructor, buffer limits and strict interior traversal. Parametric derivatives depend on the source chart; geometric G1/G2/Gsmooth policies retain their existing enum and selector values.",
    "Analytic adapter tests distinguish a straight locus with a speed jump from one with a pure second-derivative jump. They cover affine chart changes and negative homogeneous gauges. Sources rejected by native NURBS validation, including full-order interior knots, return errors rather than empty continuity results.",
    "The 64 frozen profile sets compare original, shifted-domain, degree 3 and degree 5representations in both directions and at two fit tolerances. Native source inspection also retains simplified PolylineCurve definitions, C1/G1/G2 breaks and limiting derivatives on owned duplicates.",
    "All 768 continuity and 1,024 limiting-derivative comparisons match within 1e-9. Existing geometric region and surface-crease regressions remain passing; two pre-existing raw/near-tie diagnostics remain ignored.",
    "Native fitted definitions remain invariant within 1e-9 under tested degree elevation, affine charts and polyline simplification. All measured sources have one C1 break and no G1/G2 breaks; the existence of a C1 break alone does not determine the varying fitted topology.",
    "No subdivision heuristic was admitted. A separate fixed-topology prototype interpolating nine measured length parameters reconstructs the two tight default-clock control nets to about 1e-15, but fails other source clocks. It uses native target knots and is not a qualified adaptive algorithm."
  ],
